<title>PORTUGAL: Portugal industrial prices rose 3.7 pct yr/yr in Oct. [CORRECTED 12:03 gmt]</title>
<headline>Portugal industrial prices rose 3.7 pct yr/yr in Oct. [CORRECTED 12:03 gmt]</headline>
<dateline>LISBON 1996-12-20</dateline>
<text>
<p>Portugal's index of industrial producer prices rose 3.7 percent year-on-year in October, while month-on-month it rose 0.5 percent. the National Statistics Institute (INE) said.</p>
<p>(Corrects to make clear index relates to industrial producer prices).</p>
<p>					 Oct 96	Sep 96	Oct 95</p>
<p>General Index			121.3	  120.8	 117.1</p>
<p>Percentage change yr/yr	   +3.7	   +2.9</p>
<p>Percentage change mo/mo	   +0.5	   +0.1</p>
<p>Accumulated 12 months	     +3.0	   +3.0</p>
<p>Base Year = 1985  </p>
<p>The following is a sectoral breakdown:</p>
<p>Mining				 117.9	  117.8	 116,6</p>
<p>Manufacturing			118.9	  118.2	 113.2</p>
<p>Electricity, gas, water	  135.0	  135.0	 137.5</p>
<p>Food, drink, tobacco	     122.2	  124.5	 118.7</p>
<p>Textile				117.1	  117.1	 117.5</p>
<p>--Lisbon bureau 3511-3150035</p>
</text>
